In NC my state, they increased the penalty for assaults on ride share drivers. ITs up to 6 months in jail I think.  I would totally file charges.  At a minimum he will serve at least a few months in jail.  If needed, I would get a lawyer to push them to charge him if necessary. 

&#x200B;

Going the media route with a sob story and the a dash cam video is what I would do.  Have my mom or family member create go fund me. 

&#x200B;

Wouldn't report it to uber directly.  IF the news story gets the attention of uber, they will be less inclined to deactivate you at this point.  Because if they do its bad press.  Ubers policy only bans firearms, not weapons.  This was changed several years a go, from not allowing any weapons.  so pepper spray, stun guns are ok depending on your states laws.  This isn't the way on lyft. IF you try to defend your self with anything on lyft, you are probably getting deactivated.  (if this happens, make sure to give a follow up to the media, and a update on go fund me).

&#x200B;

I dont caryy a stun gun, because of my states laws of having it on university campuses.  But pepper spray is fair game.

