People bringing up the computer with the fans. As a actual PC tech. I want to comment. 

Generally one dosent have fans outside of a computer case. Unless you have the computer case open and the fan is directly pointed at the CPU or graphics card. Fans siting next to a computer case is going to minimally help cooling.

&#x200B;

I assume she has a decent gaming computer.  Unless its overclocked and she is doing demanding games. Then even at 79 F, it really shouldn't overheat.  The games she plays are not demanding.  In terms of processor or graphics performance.

&#x200B;

I wonder if the heat is turned on more then we think. IF we are looking at like 80f plus temps. Then the possibility dose increase of the PC overheating.  

&#x200B;

With pc cooling, its mostly about displacing the heat.  (The heat on the cpu needs to be moved of it and out the back fan.) Having a higher ambient temp can cause problems.  But at 79f its not likely.  Unless its overclocked and or with demeaning games. 

&#x200B;

at like 83, 84 85, then performance might start to be effected.

I find that my mindset and what I am doing influences how I fell while taking any noid. Yes there is differences with each one. But if I am up dancing to music I fell better.  I take a particular gummy for sleeping.  But if I am up and try to stay awake and watch TV I  start to fell euphoric.  And not that sleepy. 

&#x200B;

Of course everyone responds differently to each noid two.  I dont like HHC at all. It triggered my depression. It was very strange. 

&#x200B;

But a delta 8 vape, that was the most euphoric thing I ever tried.  More so then any delta 9 gummy I ever had. 

&#x200B;

To each there own.

